<title>ITALY: SPECIALISTS BID FOR 193 BLN LIRE ITALY 18-MO CTZ.</title>
<headline>SPECIALISTS BID FOR 193 BLN LIRE ITALY 18-MO CTZ.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 193 billion lire of 24-month zero coupon certificates (CTZ) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 150 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 3.10 trillion lire at the open auction for the July 15, 1999 paper, against 1.50 trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 89.20 from 89.25 at the previous CTZ sale on July 20.</p>
</text>
